<title>USA: PRIMUS files for $125 mln debt offer.</title>
<headline>PRIMUS files for $125 mln debt offer.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>PRIMUS Telecommunications Group Inc on Friday said it filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission for a public offering of $125 million in senior notes and warrants to purchase common stock.</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers will manage the offering, PRIMUS said.</p>
<p>PRIMUS is a multinational telecommunications company that focuses on the provision of international and domestic long-distance services.</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1672))</p>
